$7B3E AN OPERATION: ITS RESULT IS IN THE ACCUMULATOR
$7B4C A SINGLE OPERAND: LOADING IT SETS THE FLAGS
$7B52 A SINGLE INTEGER OPERAND STAYS AN INTEGER UNLESS A REAL IS WANTED
$7B7E LOAD IT
$7B81 AN INTEGER RESULT WHERE A REAL IS WANTED: FLOAT IT (ENTRY 131)
$7B9F THE TARGET IS A SIMPLE VARIABLE
$7BAD AN ARRAY ELEMENT: A VALUE FOR AN INTEGER ARRAY THAT IS NOT ALREADY AN INTEGER (FROM INPUT, READ, GET OR A REAL EXPRESSION) IS MADE AN INTEGER (ENTRY 1, AYINT)
$7BE2 THEN ENTRY 67 STORES IT AT THE ELEMENT'S ADDRESS
$7BE8 (THE CALL)
$7BEB OPERATION 1 STORES THE ACCUMULATOR ...
$7BF1 ... OPERATION 7 STORES THE FLOATING POINT ACCUMULATOR IN AN INTEGER VARIABLE
$7C26 THE TARGET'S SYMBOL
$7C2C REMEMBER A PLAIN STORE: A LOAD OF THE SAME VARIABLE RIGHT AFTER IT IS LEFT OUT
$7C46 A STRING VARIABLE NEEDS NO MASK
$7C57 (EMIT THE STORE)
$7C5A ENTRY: LOAD THE RIGHT OPERAND ...
$7C60 ENTRY: ... OR {OX}, UNLESS IT IS ALREADY IN THE ACCUMULATOR (OPERATION 0, KEEPING {K})
$7C86 ENTRY: APPLY {OX} WITH OPERATION {K}: ITS SYMBOL ...
$7C95 ... AND KIND
$7CA4 A TEMPORARY IS FREE AGAIN ONCE IT IS USED
$7CCD A STRING LITERAL: JSR TO ENTRY 36 AND THE LITERAL'S ADDRESS
$7CFC AN INTEGER USED AS A REAL TAKES THE OPERATION+6; AN INTEGER CONSTANT IS REPLACED BY ITS REAL FORM, ENTERED NOW IF NEEDED
$7D69 A LOAD (OR AND/OR TEST) OF THE VARIABLE JUST STORED IS LEFT OUT WHEN THE STORE WAS THE LAST CODE WRITTEN
$7DAE STRING VARIABLES AND TEMPORARIES NEED NO MASK
$7DD4 A LOAD OR OTHER OPERATION, MARKED IN THE MASK
$7DE2 AN AND / OR TEST: OPERATION 20
$7DE5 AN INTEGER TAKES THREE MORE BYTES FOR THE ORA OF ITS SECOND BYTE (PASS 2 FILLS THEM IN)
$7DF9 A REAL: LDA $9D (THE EXPONENT IS ZERO ONLY FOR ZERO)
$7E0A AN INTEGER: LDA $A0 ...
$7E13 ... ORA $A1
$7E1C END THE DIRECT FILE OUTPUT
$7E1F CLOSE ALL FILES
$7E28 AND DELETE THE UNFINISHED OBJECT FILE
$7E55 (THE FILES STAY CLOSED)
$7E82 PUT BACK THE SIX BYTES OF DOS THAT PASS 0 CHANGED
$7E93 THE ADDRESS AND THE ORIGINAL BYTE
$7EB6 OPEN AND CLOSE THE LINE NUMBER FILE; THE PROGRAM ENDS HERE
